"Zwicky's puzzle ({#}). The galaxies in this cluster move at about {#} km/s along our line of sight. Here only the stars pull, {#}% of the mass. Press Play: the galaxies fly apart in a billion years or so, yet real clusters are billions of years old and still together. Something unseen must hold them.",
